File Index

/autoleveling-actions.ts
Purpose: Parses and serializes autoleveling action scripts to/from the one-line-per-action editor format. Action kinds incl. send, send_cooldown (`cooldown <sec> <cmd>`), send_every_ticks (`every_ticks <n> <cmd>` — recast every N GMCP ticks, for affect-less buffs), wait_ms/text/regex/fighting, if_hp/mp/mv_below, if_affect_missing.

/autoleveling-alignment.ts
Purpose: alignmentXpModifier(player, target) — the DSL-customized XP rule (opposite alignment 2×, same 0.5×, any-neutral / unknown 1×). The engine divides observed tnl-drops by it to get a base kill-XP figure, then re-applies it for the "near a level-up" prediction. Alignment types live in autoleveling-types.ts (AutoLevelAlignment); the wizard captures them (not in GMCP).

/autoleveling-buff-catalog.ts
Purpose: BUFF_CATALOG — log-verified command↔GMCP-affect-name pairs for the common leveling buffs (sanc→sanctuary, stone→stone skin, fren→frenzy, 'detect inv'→detect invis, …). Consumed by CombatStep's "Add from catalog". Entries carry suggestInCombat (sanctuary is item-only in combat) / suggestHoldNearLevel (haste hurts mana regen); Berserk has affect:'' (no GMCP affect → tick gate).

/autoleveling-content-types.ts
Purpose: DTOs for the C#-served content — AutoPilotAreaSummary (index row), AutoPilotArea (detail: route dirs, level range, start room/speedwalk, recommendedTargets), AutoPilotTarget, AND the class catalog: AutoPilotClass ({name, mortalClass, isReclass, classGroup, abilities}) + AutoPilotAbility ({name, type skill|spell|song, level, groups[] — semantic IAbilityGroup names since IAbility.Usage/Duration/Group are unpopulated, helpFile?}). Mirrors Server.Dsl/Models/Autopilot.cs. normalizeAreaSummary / normalizeArea / normalizeClass / normalizeAbility COERCE rather than type-guard (C# serializer omits false/0/""). Buffs / fight scripts are NOT here — wizard-time client overlay in autoleveling-user-data.ts.

/autoleveling-classes.ts
Purpose: Read-through IndexedDB cache (shatteredarchive-maps DB, key autolevelingClasses, 7d soft TTL, network→cache fallback) of GET /api/web/maps/autoleveling/classes — getClassCatalog({force?}) + getClassCatalogCached(). Pure helpers: classByName (case-insensitive), classNames (base classes — !isReclass — first, each half A→Z), abilitiesForClass(list, name, {atOrBelowLevel?, type?, groups?}) (groups = any-of; no filter = every ability the class has — CombatStep's buff picker uses this directly now, see below). classOffensiveAbilities (OFFENSIVE_GROUPS ∩ groups, or a known COMBAT_SKILL_NAMES skill) is the one remaining group-heuristic helper, used only by the fight-command picker. __setClassStoreForTests seam. Mirrors autoleveling-content.ts. 2026-09-13 history: a `classBuffAbilities` group-heuristic (mirroring classOffensiveAbilities) briefly existed for the buff picker but was REMOVED same day — it kept mis-categorizing real abilities (Shukenja spells leaking cross-class, Faerie Fire, Berserk) faster than the heuristic could be patched, so the buff picker now just shows every ability the selected class actually has (abilitiesForClass, no group filtering) — see CombatStep.tsx and the DSL repo's ability-classification-admin plan, which will eventually replace ALL client-side group-guessing (including classOffensiveAbilities) with a real per-ability admin-curated classification. OFFENSIVE_GROUPS (still live) includes a `SONG_GROUPS` constant (HymnsOfLife/SkaldChants/WarHymns — the server's real GroupType.Songs semantic group names, confirmed against Server.Dsl/ClassAbilityGroups/*.cs) and `'Weather'` (mostly attack spells + Faerie Fire, confirmed via ClassAbilityGroups/Weather.cs).

/autoleveling-idb.ts
Purpose: Tiny async KvStore abstraction — indexedDbKvStore(db,store) is the browser default; memoryKvStore() is the test/no-IDB drop-in. Backs the area cache and the user-data store.

/autoleveling-content.ts
Purpose: Read-through IndexedDB cache (shatteredarchive-maps DB, 7d soft TTL, network→cache fallback) of the split list/detail API — getAreaIndex() (all areas as lightweight AutoPilotAreaSummary, GET /api/web/maps/autoleveling/areas) + getAreaDetail(slug) (one area's route+targets, cached per slug). Pure helpers areasForLevel / areaBySlug / areasByContinent / isLevelInRange operate on the summary shape; fullRoute needs the detail. __setAreaStoreForTests seam. Mirrors autoleveling-maps-client.ts.

/autoleveling-user-data.ts
Purpose: Player's own auto-leveling additions in a dedicated IndexedDB DB (shatteredarchive-autoleveling/userData): custom targets (per area), buff overlays (per area), fight-command overlays (per area+class), custom paths, prefs (remembered class + player alignment), and a global per-ability learned-cooldown store (2026-09-12: getLearnedCooldown/bumpLearnedCooldown, kind 'abilityTiming', keyed by normalized command string — NOT per-area, lag is a property of the ability). Records carry id + updatedAt for profile cloud-sync (exportAll / importRecords = last-writer-wins) — step 12 wired this pair into useAccountModal.ts's Save/Load-to-cloud via cloudSync.saveAutolevelUserData/loadAutolevelUserData (api/user-content/autoleveling), the same way scripts/plugins/library already sync; see autoleveling-user-data.test.ts's export→JSON→fresh-store→import round-trip test. ensureMigrated() folds in the legacy localStorage stores (autoleveling-saved-targets, autoleveling-user-paths) once. __setUserDataStoreForTests seam. BuffRow = {label, cmd, affect? (if_affect_missing gate), refreshTicks? (tick gate), inCombatCmd? (mid-fight item action), holdNearLevel? (stop refreshing near a ding), unverified? (class-ability guess, UI hint), vitalsGate? (AutoLevelVitalsGate — optional hp/mp/mv %% precondition), onceKey? ('fight'|'round' fire-limit)}; FightRow = {cmd, cooldownSec, vitalsGate?, onceKey?}; AutoLevelPrefs = {playerClass?, playerAlignment?}.

/autoleveling-wizard-config.ts
Purpose: draftToConfig(ConfigDraft) → AutoLevelConfig (v3). Maps the wizard draft to what the engine runs: area route (fullRoute) → init.trainingPath (2026-09-12: speedwalkToStart deliberately EXCLUDED — untested bridge, deferred; player starts already at autopilot_start_room); enabled targets → init.targets; buffs → steps.start.pre (if_affect_missing / send_every_ticks / send by gate, carrying vitalsGate?/onceKey? through onto the action); buffs with inCombatCmd|holdNearLevel → config.criticalBuffs[]; fight rows → steps.fight.exec (send_cooldown/send, same vitalsGate?/onceKey? passthrough); adds a `look` to steps.identify; 3s round pause for active leveling (5-min default only for sightsee); draft.restStartOfRound/restEndOfRound (semicolon-separated commands, parseRestCommands) + restDuringRound → config.rest; draft.weightAtOrAbovePct/weightCommands (same parseRestCommands splitter, reused not duplicated) → config.weight (2026-09-13; `weightEnabled` removed same day — no separate on/off flag, a blank commands field IS off). Passes draft.playerAlignment/targetAlignment through when set. ConfigDraft is a local structural type so features/ doesn't import components/ (WizardDraft satisfies it). Buff EXECUTION is the engine's job (autoleveling-engine.ts).

/autoleveling-defaults.ts
Purpose: Default autoleveling config, disabled-by-default. AUTOLEVELING_CONFIG_VERSION = 3 (v2→v3 added criticalBuffs[]). 2026-09-13: added the default `weight` field (90%, no commands — empty commands IS off, no separate enable flag) — backfilled onto old saved configs for free by autoleveling-storage's existing top-level `{...fallback, ...src}` coerce, same as `rest` was.

/autoleveling-engine.ts
Purpose: Runtime that drives a leveling round: rest.startOfRound (wake) → steps.start (buffs) → per-segment move.pre/checkDuringRoundRest/move.post around each gated movement → injected encounters (engage → fight.pre/exec/post → recheckBuffs → postFight → clearQueueIfBuiltUp → identify re-scan) → steps.reset.endRound → rest.endOfRound → steps.reset.wait (or roundLoopTimeMs). Buff runtime: affect-gated (if_affect_missing) + tick (send_every_ticks) buffs are re-evaluated at the top of each round AND after every fight ends (recheckBuffs); "every round" bare sends fire only at round top; tick buffs fire OUT OF COMBAT only. Tracks char_data.tnl drops into a rolling kill-XP estimate — the mob's alignment is read live from the (Golden Aura)/(Red Aura) line prefix (scanMobAlignment; White/Blue/Thorn/etc. are not alignment) and normalized by alignmentXpModifier vs config.playerAlignment; while running writes a bright yellow `[auto-level] +xp · ~N kills to level …` terminal line on each gain AND (2026-09-12) reports the same numbers via deps.setXpProgress for the wizard's "Last kill" row. config.criticalBuffs on game:affect-removed → mid-fight inCombatCmd (item action, anti-flap throttle) only; the recast is recheckBuffs' job. holdNearLevel suppresses recasts once tnl ≤ the estimate. send_cooldown / vitals gates as before. 2026-09-12 additions (combat/rest tuning plan): AutoLevelVitalsGate (vitalsGateSatisfied/vitalsPct) — optional hp/mp/mv %% precondition on send/send_cooldown/send_every_ticks/if_affect_missing, checked before the kind-specific gate, missing-data never blocks; AutoLevelOnceKey 'fight'|'round' (onceGateAllows, recorded only at actual send time so a skipped kind-gate never consumes the slot); round-boundary tracking (trackRoundBoundary, debounced ROUND_GAP_MS=1000 off the shared DAMAGE_LINE_PATTERN, mirrors DslLogViewer's proven heuristic) drives both the round-scoped once-gate AND hasQueueBuildup()/commandsWithQueueBuildup (commands sent vs. rounds observed, fight-wide + per-command) — clearQueueIfBuiltUp() sends `~` only when a queue actually built up, and onAbilityCooldownLearned notifies the hook to persist a +0.5s-bumped cooldownSec per ability (autoleveling-user-data's abilityTiming store) when a fight-command's own per-command buildup fires — emitCooldownLearnedNotice writes a bright terminal "heads up" line alongside it so the change is never silent; AutoLevelRestConfig (rest.startOfRound/endOfRound run at the round's top/reset.endRound point; checkDuringRoundRest/restRuleTriggered/waitForRecovery run an out-of-combat-only threshold→sleep→poll-to-recoverTo→wake cycle, reusing endOfRound/startOfRound as the "how" — status 'resting' is a pre-existing runState variant this is the first real user of). 2026-09-13: shared `writeAutoLevelLine()` (bright-yellow "[auto-level] <body>" terminal line, factored out of emitXpProgress/emitCooldownLearnedNotice) now also fires on run-control transitions — start() ("started (<mode> mode)", or "error: <reason>" for a rejected start via a new `fail()` closure covering all 3 validation guards), stop() ("stopping..."), pause()/resume() ("paused"/"resumed", only on an actual transition — the existing early-return no-ops stay silent), a fatal round-loop error ("error: <message>"), and the final idle transition ("stopped", reached by every exit path — manual stop, natural non-looping completion, or a fatal error). Movement classification now imports classifyMovement/MOVE_DIRS from features/movement/classifyMovement.ts (shared with useCompassBlock.ts) rather than a local isMovementCommand/MOVE_DIRS copy. 2026-09-12 movement-tracking-fix Step 4: movement success/failure is now driven by the shared movementTracker's shatteredarchive:movement-succeeded/-failed events (boundOnMovementResolved), not a direct game:room-data listener that used to treat ANY arrival as success — the tracker does the real {room,sector,exits} diff. A movement-failed whose reasonLine is exactly '(timeout)' (the tracker's own head-of-queue-relative timeout) resolves as an ordinary non-fatal 'failed', same as an explicit server failure line; waitForMovement's own much-larger idleTimeoutMs timer is now a pure backstop (fatal 'timeout', stops the run) reserved for "the tracker never resolved at all." sendCommand no longer dispatches movement-attempt itself (the tracker does, off command-sent). Step 5: waitForEngageOutcome's attempt timeout is now queue-depth-aware — while movementTracker.pendingCount() > 0 at a timeout check, that time is excluded from the attempt's own elapsed budget (polled every 250ms) rather than firing, so a kill command stuck behind a movement burst gets its full attemptTimeout window measured from whenever the shared queue actually drains, not the original send instant; success/not_here resolution is untouched and fires immediately regardless of queue depth. 2026-09-12 flee-pause hardening: waitWhilePausedOrStopped() captures wasPaused and, only on an actual pause→resume transition, calls resyncAfterResume() (sendIdentifyOrLook() + delayMs(lookSettleMs)) before returning — covers every resume (flee-triggered or the manual pause/resume button) for free since it's the one choke point behind all pause-wait call sites; waitForRecovery() now suspends fully (zero action) while paused and excludes paused time from its own timeout budget, so a pause mid-rest-wait never silently "gives up" in the background. 2026-09-13 weight-gate + hot-swap/resync: charVitals gained carryWeight/carryWeightMax (GMCP carry_weight/can_carry_weight); weightPct() is a **0-fallback** (unlike vitalsPct's 100-fallback — absent data must never read as "overweight"); checkWeightGate(round) is out-of-combat only, fetches config fresh per-call (own deps.getConfig(), same pattern as checkDuringRoundRest — this is what makes it hot-swappable), edge-triggered via weightGateFired so the drop sequence fires once per threshold crossing not on every subsequent check; called from the round loop right alongside checkDuringRoundRest. Also this session: `start()`'s local `const cfg` became an instance field `this.cfg` (still fetched ONCE per run, "single consistent cfg" — NOT refactored into a per-round re-fetch) so it CAN be refreshed later; targets-normalization extracted into `refreshTargets(cfg)`; new `refreshRunSnapshot()` (`this.cfg = deps.getConfig(); refreshTargets(this.cfg);`) is called from `waitWhilePausedOrStopped()` at the same point as `resyncAfterResume()` — i.e. only on a real pause→resume transition — so targets/buffs/route/rest-start-end-of-round (which sit on the frozen `this.cfg` all run, unlike fight-commands/rest-during-round/weight which already fetch fresh) pick up a live edit via pause→edit→resume instead of a hot-swap. 2026-09-13 (live-playtest fix): auto-tuned cooldown learning is now cumulative AND live-applied within a run — `learnedCooldownSec` (per-cmd, seeded at `start()` from the persisted `abilityTiming` store via a new `deps.getLearnedCooldown`) is used as a floor under the configured `cooldownSec` for both the `send_cooldown` gate and the next bump's base, so repeated buildups climb (0→0.5→1.0→…) instead of re-deriving the same static-config-based target forever, and a cooldown learned in a past run applies from round 1 of the next one instead of re-earning it from scratch. Also 2026-09-13: `runActions()` now inserts a `lookSettleMs` delay after EACH action specifically when `stepLabel === 'start.pre'` (buffs) — that phase was the one bare-send path with zero pacing (unlike movement's moveSettleMs and fight-commands' auto-tuned cooldowns), so several buffs fired back-to-back with no regard for real cast/violence lag; traced to a live-playtest run where several buffs preceded a hard movement timeout that killed the whole run (`waitForMovement`'s backstop fires if the tracker never resolves — see movement-tracking-fix). Scoped to `start.pre` only, not a new config field — reuses the existing `lookSettleMs` knob. Also 2026-09-13 (live-playtest fix, separate report): rest.startOfRound/endOfRound `send` actions (both the natural per-round hooks AND the during-round low-vitals trigger, which reuses these same two fields — see REST_STEP_LABELS) now route through a new `sendViaCommandProcessor()` → `deps.sendThroughCommandProcessor` (hook wires it to `RuntimeSingleton.Runtime.executeAlias`, same as a manually-typed terminal line) instead of the raw literal `sendCommand()` — a rest sequence configured as the player's own alias/macro ("command stacking") was being sent to the MUD verbatim and doing nothing, since alias expansion never ran. Deliberately scoped to rest only via a `stepLabel` check inside `execAction`'s shared `send` case (same pattern as the buff-settle fix) — movement/fight-commands/buffs/weight stay on the raw path so a user's aliases can never perturb the engine's own timing-sensitive automation.

/autoleveling-index.ts
Purpose: Centralized export file for autoleveling feature with backward compatibility.

/autoleveling-maps-client.ts
Purpose: Provides cached and remote loading of autoleveling map data with IndexedDB storage.

/autoleveling-mudlet-import.ts
Purpose: Imports and converts Mudlet leveling script data into buildable path steps.

/autoleveling-normalize.ts
Purpose: Config repair + migration. `normalizeAutoLevelConfig` (currently unused) repairs old/broken shapes + old `enabled:bool`→`mode`. `migrateAutoLevelConfigV2ToV3` (used by autoleveling-storage) carries a v2 blob forward: same shape + version:3 + criticalBuffs:[].

/autoleveling-saved-targets.ts
Purpose: Stores and manages manually entered auto-leveling targets per game zone in local storage.

/autoleveling-storage.ts
Purpose: Per-connection config persistence in localStorage. Key `autoleveling-config-v3:<connId>`; hard-gates version 3. On a v3 miss it reads the old `autoleveling-config-v2:` key, migrates forward (migrateAutoLevelConfigV2ToV3), and re-saves under v3. coerceConfig fills missing fields from the default.

/autoleveling-text.ts
Purpose: Processes and normalizes text input for autoleveling functionality.

/autoleveling-types.ts
Purpose: Persisted config schema (v3) + runtime runState types. AutoLevelConfig carries criticalBuffs[], playerAlignment/targetAlignment (AutoLevelAlignment, absent = neutral), the step triplets, a required `rest` (AutoLevelRestConfig, 2026-09-12) and `weight` (AutoLevelWeightConfig, 2026-09-13 — {enabled, atOrAbovePct, commands: AutoLevelAction[]}, ONE rule not an array like Rest's duringRound; `commands` is parsed AutoLevelAction[] in the final config, same as Rest's start/end-of-round — the raw semicolon-string only lives in the wizard draft), and timing knobs. AutoLevelStepConfig no longer has the dead `trainingPath` field — the route is init.trainingPath. Actions incl. send_every_ticks, plus (2026-09-12) optional vitalsGate (AutoLevelVitalsGate: stat hp|mp|mv, op above|below, pct) and onceKey (AutoLevelOnceKey: 'fight'|'round') on send/send_cooldown/send_every_ticks/if_affect_missing — both are engine-composable preconditions, distinct from the older single-purpose if_hp/mp/mv_pct_below kinds which predate the wizard and stay as-is. AutoLevelRestConfig = {startOfRound, endOfRound: AutoLevelAction[], duringRound: AutoLevelRestDuringRoundRule[]}; a rule ({hp?,mp?,mv?,recoverTo}) requires ALL present thresholds to trigger. AutoLevelXpProgress is a separate piece of state (not on AutoLevelRunState) so it survives status transitions. Alignment math is in autoleveling-alignment.ts.

/autoleveling-user-paths.ts
Purpose: Manages user-created training paths for auto-leveling features with local storage persistence and JSON export/import functionality.
